01-6103b07b-a897-456e-b810-468551d9735e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-236_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d76562af-5785-4ef5-899c-57d3a1e383f5","comments":[],"created_at":1787185925190577001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"135eaeb1-1db6-45da-b510-6a0a65cbe093","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d1fb-cdeb-f3cf-4cd9"},{"link_uuid":"5863e0fe-e022-4f52-8bb2-e31a958be455","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"672d-62bb-4bef-4ed2"}],"description":"## What\n\nWiden `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:45`) to\n`\\[(?:non-codebase|operator-attested)\\]`, and widen the `.rebar/criteria_routing.json:75`\nactivation trigger `text_all` to match either spelling.\n\n## Why this is the keystone\n\nFIVE consumers share the IDENTICAL compiled regex object, so one pattern change propagates to\nall of them with no new branch anywhere. Four read it with normal semantics — `decide_ops`,\n`workflow_ops`, `det_attestation_launder`, `det_measurement_provenance` (each satisfies `is`\nagainst `det_operator_attested._OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE`).\n\nThe FIFTH is `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:544-547` (`ensure_ac_boxes_checked`), and its semantics\nare INVERTED: a match REMOVES an unchecked AC line from the set that blocks a ticket close\n(`offenders = [ln for ln in floor.unchecked_ac_lines if not _OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE.match(ln)]`).\nWidening the matcher therefore also makes an unchecked `[non-codebase]`-tagged AC close-exempt.\nThat is INTENDED — the exemption is the tag's whole purpose and must reach both spellings or the\nrename would silently strip it — but it is a close-gate behavior change, so it is stated here and\npinned by an AC below rather than left implicit.\n\nBecause no new branch is introduced anywhere, `det_floor.py` (793/800 LOC cap) and\n`decide_ops.plan_review_decide` (complexity 21, grandfathered) need no edits and their gates do\nnot fire.\n\n## Vocabulary is defined before code accepts it\n\nADR-0043 makes exact-token matching a deliberate FAIL-SAFE: anything that is not the exact tag is\ntreated as codebase-verifiable, so a garbled tag falls back to the STRICTER bar. Accepting a\nsecond spelling relaxes that fail-safe, so the relaxation must be a recorded decision, not an\nundocumented one. This story therefore DEPENDS ON S8 (ADR 0101), which defines `[non-codebase]`,\nrecords why `operator` mis-signalled, and states that `[operator-attested]` is retained as an\nundocumented alias. S8 lands first; this story implements the decision S8 records.\n\n## Trap\n\nThe alternation MUST be non-capturing. `decide_ops.operator_attested_ac_texts` uses `findall()`,\nwhich returns TUPLES if the group captures, silently breaking Pass-3 enrichment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` matches `- [ ] [non-codebase] x` and `- [ ] [operator-attested] x`\n      case-insensitively, and does NOT match the `[operator_attested]` underscore near-miss.\n- [x] `operator_attested_ac_texts` returns a `list[str]` (not tuples) for a description mixing\n      both spellings, proved by a test asserting element types.\n- [x] The `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` `project.measurement-provenance` trigger fires on a\n      plan tagged `[non-codebase]` and on one tagged `[operator-attested]`, proved by a test.\n- [x] An unchecked `- [ ] [non-codebase] …` AC item is EXEMPT from the `ensure_ac_boxes_checked`\n      close block exactly as an `[operator-attested]` one is, and an unchecked UNTAGGED item\n      still blocks — pinning the inverted-semantics consumer at `txn.py:547`.\n- [x] ADR 0101 (S8) is landed and defines `[non-codebase]` before this matcher accepts it.\n- [x] All existing tests pass unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py","reason":"widen the canonical tag regex to a non-capturing alternation"},{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"widen the measurement-provenance text_all activation trigger"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py","reason":"dual-match, near-miss and findall-arity tests"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck.py","reason":"close-gate exemption parity for the inverted-semantics consumer at txn.py:547"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","d1fb-cdeb-f3cf-4cd9"],["parent","6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30"],["relates_to","672d-62bb-4bef-4ed2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","parent_status_uuid":"66953a07-f262-407c-8908-377ef2e744bf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83","ticket_type":"story","title":"S1 — widen the canonical tag matcher to accept [non-codebase] and [operator-attested]","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["390bb540-2469-4fc3-8c95-b9f9506996b1","d73f4a99-2012-43e2-bc8d-ffedf55ea3e0","135eaeb1-1db6-45da-b510-6a0a65cbe093","d687cf03-f80a-4ce2-bd3a-6c8851bc4f28","b076e6ce-31d6-46c6-a858-c85fe483318a","f6fa7036-4eb7-4eb3-a36d-df19d8f2255d","afe97fd6-279e-4838-a85b-32f8cc6cc5f5","5863e0fe-e022-4f52-8bb2-e31a958be455","2c8bf3a0-5fb4-4a9b-8413-51dddb7ede21","b9a1105d-e181-4ade-b808-50d4becdd573","66953a07-f262-407c-8908-377ef2e744bf","6103b07b-a897-456e-b810-468551d9735e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787201673441857001,"uuid":"bb713fdc-2df9-4800-8488-cdd6eb52db91"}